        },
        {
          "event_type": "nothing",
          "message": "Incense drifts from a passing junk. In the East Indies, even the air is cultivated.",
          "hull_delta": 0,
          "provision_delta": 0,
          "silver_delta": 0,
          "crew_delta": 0,
          "speed_modifier": 1.0,
          "cargo_lost": [],
          "flavor": "[weather]"
        },
        {
          "event_type": "nothing",
          "message": "The light in the East Indies is different from anywhere else — softer, greener, filtered through atmospheric moisture that hasn't quite dried. It makes everything look like a painting of itself.",
          "hull_delta": 0,
          "provision_delta": 0,
          "silver_delta": 0,
          "crew_delta": 0,
          "speed_modifier": 1.0,
          "cargo_lost": [],
          "flavor": "[weather]"
        },
        {
          "event_type": "nothing",
          "message": "[bold]You arrive at Monsoon Reach.[/bold]\n\nThe port is blooming. Literally — flowers on the docks, garlands on the warehouses, the scent of jasmine mixing with salt air. Spring arrivals in the East Indies feel like being invited to a celebration of survival.\n\nThe harbor curves around a headland crowned by the Wind Temple. Ships here are built with deeper keels and stronger masts — the monsoon demands it.\n\n[bold]Harbor Master Ravi:[/bold] \"Welcome. The wind is from the southeast today — good for arrivals, not for departures. You'll berth at the headland. The monks will post tomorrow's forecast at dawn.\"\n\n[dim]Landmark: The Wind Temple — a pagoda on the headland where monks track the monsoon.[/dim]\n[dim]Custom: Captains consult the monks before sailing. Their wind forecasts are uncannily accurate.[/dim]",
          "hull_delta": 0,
          "provision_delta": 0,
          "silver_delta": 0,
          "crew_delta": 0,
          "speed_modifier": 1.0,
          "cargo_lost": [],
          "flavor": "[arrival]"
        }
